~ start
Concertgoer: I didn't expect to see you here. You been here all day?
You: Yeah, since the afternoon. It's been a good one.
Concertgoer: Same. Hey, I grabbed something earlier if you want any. It makes the whole thing hit way different.
You: What is it?
Concertgoer: Just something to take the edge off. Half the people here are on it right now, it's nothing crazy.
You: I don't know...
Concertgoer: Seriously, you'll thank me when the lights drop. It just makes everything feel more alive. You're already here, might as well actually feel it.
- Nah, I'm good. I'm already feeling the energy in here.
    => choice_a
- Maybe later in the night.
    => choice_b
- Okay... yeah, sure.
    => choice_c
- I'll pass. But do you actually know what's in it?
    => choice_d

~ choice_a
Concertgoer: Your loss. (shrugs and turns back to the stage)
You: (to yourself) Huh. That was it.
Narrator: The lights drop. The crowd surges forward. You are completely present for all of it.
System: Skill reinforced: Values-based refusal. You don't owe anyone an explanation. Naming what you're already feeling makes the "no" land without any drama.
=> END

~ choice_b
Concertgoer: Yeah for sure, just find me after the first few songs.
Narrator: The set starts. Twenty minutes in, the Concertgoer taps you on the shoulder.
Concertgoer: So — still maybe later, or you actually want some now?
You: (realizes the door is still open)
System: Skill reinforced: "Maybe later" delays the pressure but doesn't end it. A clear "no" upfront costs less than carrying the decision through the whole night.
=> END

~ choice_c
Concertgoer: There you go. (hands it over) You'll feel it in a bit.
Narrator: The set starts. You wait. Then something shifts — the crowd feels too close, the sound too loud.
You: (to yourself) I don't actually know what I just took.
Narrator: The Concertgoer has disappeared into the crowd. You are alone with it.
System: Skill reinforced: If anything feels wrong, find event medical staff immediately. That is not overreacting — it is exactly what they are there for, and you will not get in trouble.
=> END

~ choice_d
Concertgoer: (pause) The guy said it was fine.
You: Yeah but like — do you actually know?
=> END